  clock: 1  # 3b4d
  nonce: 3b4d  # 3b4d
  data:  # 3b4d
    kind: work_item  # 3b4d
    title: "validation_report violations_by_class all=0 despite 6644+ enumerable cross_field defects"  # 3b4d
    status: todo_hard  # 3b4d
    priority: 1  # 3b4d
    parent: INV-luhur-sital-lonar-tagiv-kuzab-mokol-jikot-fosug  # 3b4d
    tags:  # 3b4d
    - dogfood_tranch_03  # 3b4d
    - dogfood  # 3b4d
    isbefore: []  # 3b4d
    duplicate_of: []  # 3b4d
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 3b4d
    pr_ref:  # 3b4d
    description: "**Mechanic**: The validation report exposes buckets `axis_conformance`, `cross_field`, `id_format`, `verdict_enum`, `writer_contract`, all reporting 0 defects. Direct substrate scan finds 492 dangling-pass-id violations (cross-field), 4,507 :unresolved-with-is_resolved=True violations (cross-field), 1,645 empty-origin violations (cross-field), and others. Either the validation rules are not wired to check these classes, or the report is generated against a frozen rule set that pre-dates the check categories.\n\n**Expectation**: `cross_field` and `id_format` counters reflect real violations in the substrate, or the report names which rules are wired (so a zero count signals \"no instances of the rules that exist\", not \"no instances of any cross-field defect\").\n\n**Scope**: All five `violations_by_class` counters report zero on the self-corpus; multiple cross-field defects in the same substrate are enumerable from a direct scan.\n\n**Exposure**: Any consumer reading `violations_by_class.cross_field=0` and concluding the substrate is clean on that dimension.\n\n**Consequence**: Consumers are led to believe whole defect classes are absent when they are merely unchecked; the validation report's apparent passing grade is misleading.\n\n**Source**: F51.A3 (INDEPENDENT, HIGH).\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # 3b4d
    fields: {}  # 3b4d
